<task id="175" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Stored Secure and Access Permission follow the parent both ways for filed work assignments and projects, and are locked while a parent exists: un-securing cascades, permission changes cascade, the secure/unsecure commands and the field are unavailable on a child (owner round 84, replaces round 6 item 4)</title>
    <phase>Session 27 — UAC defect remediation (owner round 84, 2026-10-08)</phase>
    <gate>startable after task 174 merges (enforcement already follows the parent, so a lagging stored flag is never a hole)</gate>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes the secure/unsecure write paths, the inheritance job, container moves on unsecure, ribbon/forms, and tests.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive and high blast radius: it reverses an owner rule (round 6 item 4), changes task 158's inheritance and the unsecure endpoint, and moves documents between containers.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits SecureRootInheritance/SecureRootInheritanceJob, UnsecureProjectEndpoint and the AccessRibbons; live ribbon/form writes must not interleave with task 173's form script.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>174</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, dataverse, ribbon, forms, job, testing, deploy</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Owner round 84 (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md): "Child access should always follow parent; if parent changes, then child changes. A protection is that if a child has a parent then the access cannot be changed manually (e.g. its locked)." Follow-ups: un-securing cascades ("Child follows"); applies to work assignments and projects ("all children").</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make the STORED sprk_issecure and sprk_accesspermission of every filed work assignment and project equal its parents' effective values (task 174's rule), in both directions and on every change. Lock them while the record has a parent: in the UI (field and commands) and on the server (the secure/unsecure endpoints refuse a child with a parent).</prompt>

  <amendments source="main session, 2026-10-08 (task 067 verifier pass 2)" binding="true">
    <amendment>Manage Access modal lock for a child with a parent (AccessGrantModal + TrackingFieldTrio host):
- Hide or disable + Contact / + Organization / + User, candidate approve, level dropdowns, Suggested Access Grant/Dismiss and Revoke.
- Show a banner "Access follows the parent {type/name}; manage it there", linking to the parent.
- can-manage-access (or the modal) distinguishes "locked: follows parent" from "no permission".
- classifyAccessFailure maps the new 409 access_follows_parent to a designed message.
- The host's Access Permission pill is read-only on a child (accessPermissionDisabled).
- Inherited grants are a read-only row kind (new provenance value + classifyCurrentAccessRow branch), with the veto and cancellation markers still applied.
- describeCoverage wording follows 064's contract.
- Tests for a locked child.
- PCF version bump per the pcf-deploy skill.</amendment>
  </amendments>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: .NET 10 BFF secure transitions (inheritance job, unsecure endpoint, SPE container moves), Dataverse ribbon and form XML, PowerShell operator scripts.</role>

  <goal>(1) DOWNWARD CASCADE ON EVERY CHANGE.
- When a parent becomes Secure, its filed work assignments and projects become Secure. The existing inheritance does this (SecureIfFiledUnderSecureAsync / SecureRootInheritanceJob); keep it.
- When a parent becomes NOT secure, its filed children whose only secure source was that parent become not secure through the same server path as /unsecure-project: ownership back to the business unit and documents back to the business-unit container. This is new; it replaces round 6 item 4.
- When a parent's sprk_accesspermission changes, the children's value is updated to the effective value.
- A child with another secure or more restrictive ancestor keeps the most restrictive value.
(2) RE-FILE. Moving a child under a different parent, or removing its parent, recomputes its stored values. A child left with no parent keeps its last values and becomes editable.
(3) THE CASCADE RUNS through the existing scheduled jobs (SecureRootInheritanceJob, plus the secure-child reconcile where it fits). No new timer. It converges within the existing cycle. Idempotent; writes only where a value differs; resumable after a fault.
(4) LOCK.
- POST secure / make-secure, /unsecure-project, and any route that sets sprk_accesspermission on a work assignment or project refuse a record that has a parent, with a named 409 code (e.g. access_follows_parent) naming the parent.
- The Access ribbon hides Make Secure / Remove Secure on such records.
- The forms show sprk_accesspermission read-only with an "inherited from {parent}" notification (same mechanism as task 173's script).
- Parentless records are unchanged: F3 still applies to them.
(5) SAFETY.
- An un-secure cascade never leaves a child secure-flagged with its documents moved out, or the reverse: the same ordering and rollback guarantees as /unsecure-project (task 158).
- S5 (a secure record keeps a reader) and round 76 (Restricted wins) still hold.
- Every step fails closed: if a step cannot complete, the child stays at the MORE restrictive state and is reported.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Task 174 makes enforcement follow the parent whatever the stored flags say. This task makes the stored flags and the UI agree, so users see the truth and cannot set a child's access by hand. Task 173 does the same for the Access Permission of To Do, Event, Communication and Document.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Access/SecureRootInheritance.cs, SecureRootInheritanceJob.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs (container move, ownership, rollback) and the make-secure route (find it: ProvisionProjectEndpoint / secure endpoints)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Access/SecureChildReconciliationJob.cs</file>
      <file>infrastructure/dataverse/ribbon/AccessRibbons/ (Set-AccessRibbon.ps1, access-group.template.xml; enable rules)</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/tasks/158-secure-inherit-filed-work-assignment-project.poml and its notes (constraints this task supersedes)</file>
      <file>Task 173's form-lock script (reuse it for the work assignment and project forms if 173 has merged; otherwise coordinate)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="round 84">Supersedes round 6 item 4 and task 158's "no unsecure cascade" constraint. Record that in the notes; change no other task-158 behaviour.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036 / ADR-052">Use the existing scheduled jobs; no new BackgroundService or timer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §17">No plugin. One server-side owner per invariant: the cascade lives in one service called from the job and the transition endpoints.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No app-setting, Entra or Key Vault changes. Container moves only through the existing broker paths (task 171). Live ribbon/form -Apply runs are main-session gates.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/jobs.md</file>
