  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read rounds 6, 82-84 and task 158's notes. Inventory every path that sets sprk_issecure or sprk_accesspermission on a work assignment or project.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement the cascade service (secure, unsecure and permission; recomputed on re-file) and call it from the jobs and the transition endpoints.</step>
    <step order="3">Endpoint refusals (409 access_follows_parent).</step>
    <step order="4">Ribbon enable rules and the form lock; scripts with dry run / -Apply / -Verify.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests, full suites, publish delta, PR. Update TASK-INDEX and the POML status; run the drift check.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If an un-secure cascade would move documents for a child that holds external grants or JIT writers in a way /unsecure-project itself refuses, STOP and report the case.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a child has two parents with conflicting secure states and the stored-value rule is ambiguous beyond "most restrictive", STOP.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">The files in relevant-files</output>
    <output type="test">Tests beside the SecureRootInheritance, UnsecureProjectEndpoint and reconcile tests</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-175-child-access-cascade.md; docs/architecture/uac-access-control.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Unsecuring matter M (by an allowed user) leaves, within one job cycle, every work assignment and project filed only under M not secure, owned by the BU, with its documents in the BU container; a child also under another secure parent stays secure.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Changing M from Standard to Restricted (and back) updates its filed children's sprk_accesspermission within one cycle; rows already correct are not written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Re-filing a child from secure M to non-secure N makes it not secure (cascade path); removing its parent keeps its values and makes them editable.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST make-secure, POST /unsecure-project and any Access Permission write on a child with a parent return 409 access_follows_parent naming the parent; on a parentless record they behave as before (F3 unchanged).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On the forms, Make Secure / Remove Secure are hidden and Access Permission is read-only with the "inherited from" notification on a child with a parent; -Verify passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A fault mid-cascade leaves each affected child at the more restrictive state, reports it, and the next run completes it; no child is left flagged secure with its documents moved out, or the reverse.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the cases above, plus one seeding proof for the fail-closed ordering of the un-secure cascade. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification. Full suites pass; publish delta recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">LIVE GATE (dev): secure a throwaway matter with a filed work assignment, unsecure the matter, and confirm the work assignment follows (flag, owner, container) and that the commands are hidden on it; clean up.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Locked on a filed work assignment">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a work assignment filed under a secure matter</step>
        <step>Verify Make Secure / Remove Secure are not offered and Access Permission is read-only with the parent named</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Locked and labelled; dark mode adapts; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

